ces?"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"Werecommend","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":526.6487905639306,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":28.3464,"r":179.8524,"t":542.1298046484376},"charspan":[0,11],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/3","text":"Werecommend"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Creating streets that are principally defined by the position of buildings rather than the route of the carriageway.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":476.14970809671337,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":28.346299999999985,"r":254.21640000000002,"t":510.85980464843755},"charspan":[0,116],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/4","text":"Creating streets that are principally defined by the position of buildings rather than the route of the carriageway."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Designing building that turn corners well , so that both elevations seen from the street have windows to them, rather than offering blank walls to the street 14 . Consider using windows that wrap around corners to maximise surveillance and bring generous amounts of natural light into people's homes.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":385.14970809671337,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":28.346199999999982,"r":276.2849,"t":458.85980464843755},"charspan":[0,300],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/5","text":"Designing building that turn corners well , so that both elevations seen from the street have windows to them, rather than offering blank walls to the street 14 . Consider using windows that wrap around corners to maximise surveillance and bring generous amounts of natural light into people's homes."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Using a pattern of road types to create a hierarchy of streets and consider their enclosure, keeping to the well proportioned height to width ratios relative to the type of street 15 .","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":320.1497080967133,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":28.346099999999865,"r":271.6960999999999,"t":367.85980464843755},"charspan":[0,184],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/6","text":"Using a pattern of road types to create a hierarchy of streets and consider their enclosure, keeping to the well proportioned height to width ratios relative to the type of street 15 ."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Source: Manual for Streets (2007) p.54 Respecting basic design principles when designing layouts. For example, forming strong perimeter blocks. 16","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":203.1497080967133,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":36.850500000000096,"r":271.28679999999997,"t":237.8598046484375},"charspan":[0,146],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/7","text":"Source: Manual for Streets (2007) p.54 Respecting basic design principles when designing layouts. For example, forming strong perimeter blocks. 16"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","enumerated":false,"label":"list_item","marker":"","orig":"7b Good buildings 'turn' corners. Do buildings turn corners well?","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":631.9755684415412,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":308.97652999999997,"r":479.4985299999998,"t":654.5566946484378},"charspan":[0,65],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/8","text":"7b Good buildings 'turn' corners. Do buildings turn corners well?"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","enumerated":false,"label":"list_item","marker":"","orig":"7c Do all fronts of buildings, including front doors, face the street?","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":592.9755084415413,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":308.9765299999998,"r":498.1665199999999,"t":615.5566346484378},"charspan":[0,70],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/9","text":"7c Do all fronts of buildings, including front doors, face the street?"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Orientating front doors to fac